            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "epollnow"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I substituted Feta cheese instead and roasted the pecans slightly in a pan for a few minutes before adding to the rest. Really tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-15T22:29:21.483Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laura"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was afraid the dressing was going to be too sweet when I first made it, but it turned out terrific. Improvised with lettuce and feta cheese, and toasted the pecans in the oven with a little cinnamon, nutmeg, sugar water coating. YUMMY and so simple.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-09T19:50:26.270Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "robin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made pretty much as recipe stated. Did add sliced raw mushrooms and used walnuts instead of pecans. Served the dressing on the side, but maybe add it to salad right before serving.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-11T01:23:17.003Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessica Hill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Truly an excellent salad. Definitely do toast the nuts beforehand (I used both pecans and walnuts). I also subbed goat cheese for the Gorgonzola and reduced the honey to 1.5 Tbsp in the dressing. Fantastic for summer.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-05T10:36:41.803Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LolaMama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! Toasted pecans are so much better than raw - you really must take the time to toast them. I just put them in a skillet with a little butter being careful not to burn them. Also, fine quality balsamic vinegar will change your life - honest, it will! I buy it by the ounce. Oh, so good - like fine restaurant salads!",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-03T13:03:54.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "wine lover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a simple, tasty salad. I've now made it several times. My only adjustments were that, after making it the first time, I felt it didn't need that much olive oil, so I cut that down to 1/4 cup. I also slivered the pecans and toasted them in the oven before adding them to the salad. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-08T01:26:49.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "momof5"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a delicious salad. Made it for a family gathering, and everyone loved it. I used Romaine lettuce instead of spinach, raspberries and mandarin oranges instead of strawberries, and feta cheese instead of gorgonzola. You can really adjust it to your tastes. The dressing is what makes it. I put it on right before serving, and it was perfect. Will definitely be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-01T14:51:33.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CookingLuv"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delish! I cut the balsamic vinegar in half using 1/8 c of it with 1/8c balsamic glaze. I then added red onion; slightly sautéed in a small amount of olive oil/balsamic glaze. Along with candied pecans &amp; almonds and finally fresh avocado slices a top the bed of fresh spinach. Magnific! I'm adding this delictible salad into my daily/ weekly rotation as a main &amp; side dish!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-08-14T15:00:59.387Z"
          },
          {
